<title>BELGIUM: EU experts find Boeing offers insufficient - source.</title>
<headline>EU experts find Boeing offers insufficient - source.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union antitrust experts agreed with the European Commission on Wednesday that concessions offered by Boeing to win approval for its merger with McDonnell Douglas were not enough, an EU source said.</p>
<p>However, the meeting of competition officials from the EU's 15 member states asked the European Union executive to explore possibilities for new talks with Boeing, the source said.</p>
<p>&quot;The advisory committe agreed with the Commission that the commitments offered by the parties to date are not sufficient to remedy the competition problems...and do not prevent a strengthening of Boeing's dominant position,&quot; the source said. The source was reading from a statement agreed at the meeting.</p>
<p>The European Commission is due to decide on the merger on July 23.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 2287 68 11</p>
